                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71cbe51b-4654-4a32-81e4-925c3eba9560",
                                                "sense_id": "bee7eb00-45fe-36ca-a470-b3479748271b",
                                                "text": "In a report released on Monday, the world's foremost energy watchdog, the International Energy Agency (IEA), said the US would benefit from so-called unconventional sources of oil and gas, including shale gas and shale oil, derived from fracking – blasting dense rocks apart to release the fossil fuels trapped within."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31181ae3-f1e7-462a-962b-b69059b34cb8",
                                                "sense_id": "bee7eb00-45fe-36ca-a470-b3479748271b",
                                                "text": "The shale gas boom of the past five years took the US by surprise. Gas prices there have plunged and electricity production is shifting fast from coal to gas-fired power stations. This has had a huge effect on all parts of the US economy, and is changing politics globally."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0580441-f73e-4a1b-a204-ea824a023944",
                                                "sense_id": "bee7eb00-45fe-36ca-a470-b3479748271b",
                                                "text": "The UK’s underground shale gas reserves may deliver only a fraction of the gas promised by fracking firms and government ministers, according to a study."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
